{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"rebar-debug bug 9f63: ROOT CAUSE proven — reconcile.py advanced its persisted events-log cursor to the newest event unconditionally at pass end, even when it had abandoned a candidate (check-error / review-timeout / voter error-or-deferred). ?t1= is a server-side inclusive lower bound (verified live), so an abandoned candidate left every future window permanently. Gerrit webhooks is at-MOST-once and the receiver queue is in-memory, so the reconciler is the ONLY recovery path — hence 'never voted until a human nudges it'. Both nudges work because each mints a fresh event AFTER the cursor. FIX: cursor is now a low-water mark min(newest, oldest retryably-abandoned), explicit terminal-vs-retryable partition, bounded hold-back via RECONCILE_MAX_HOLDBACK_SECONDS. Observability: /health gains queue_depth; reconcile_done gains held_back + cursor. Landed as Gerrit change 1512; LLM-Review +1 at 17:19:05 (17m58s after upload, auto-queued with NO manual nudge). Siblings filed: 6a65, b0f5. Worktree /Users/joeoakhart/rebar-dbg-9f63 branch dbg-9f63."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786124488609206001,"uuid":"3e5a9ca1-5ba9-4d95-95e3-2dd610d0f93b"}